Suddenly, the sky becomes very dark.
And heavy rain starts again.
Today, this weather is changing very quickly.
Just twenty minutes ago, the sky was completely clear.
And now these big drops of water are falling.
I quickly run inside the gates of a museum.
There is a large portico at the museum's entrance.
I stand there to escape the rain.
Outside, those people are also running here and there.
I close my umbrella and shake it out well.
Five months ago, in January, Mumbai's weather was very different.
Back then, it did not rain here at all.
But now this whole city is wet.
I adjust my clothes.
And then I quietly step inside the museum.
